    'male|a||But the rest of the structure walks into a second fate: the things no trial ever reaches.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 5880
      voice: 'gemini:Charon | a clear, warm university lecturer: measured, engaged, never theatrical #ctx:7hvjwe'
    male|a||Our Markov model runs a child treated at six months out over eighty years, from five years of evidence — nobody will ever run the study that checks that tail.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 10640
      voice: 'gemini:Charon | a clear, warm university lecturer: measured, engaged, never theatrical #ctx:tu0aui'
    'male|a||Methodological uncertainty settles there permanently: the four percent discount rate, the perspective, the threshold, whether health should be counted in QALYs at all.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 10400
      voice: 'gemini:Charon | a clear, warm university lecturer: measured, engaged, never theatrical #ctx:bco2xi'
    male|a||Heterogeneity gets a fate of its own — it is real variation, not ignorance, so it cannot shrink; you can only stop averaging and split the decision.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 10920
      voice: 'gemini:Charon | a clear, warm university lecturer: measured, engaged, never theatrical #ctx:1fxhk17'
    'male|a||Beslutningsforum, the national decision forum, did exactly that: nusinersen was rejected, then accepted with an age limit at eighteen — one technology, two answers, by subgroup.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 12120
      voice: 'gemini:Charon | a clear, warm university lecturer: measured, engaged, never theatrical #ctx:15kwpc3'
    'male|a||So box the bottom of that column: this is the residue, everything still standing after the perfect trial.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 6600
      voice: 'gemini:Charon | a clear, warm university lecturer: measured, engaged, never theatrical #ctx:7uxhls'
    male|a||Imagine that perfect trial has been run — ten thousand infants, thirty years of follow-up, every parameter nailed down.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 7560
      voice: 'gemini:Charon | a clear, warm university lecturer: measured, engaged, never theatrical #ctx:cw694k'
    male|a||You would know the QALY gain to three decimals, and still not know these three.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 5480
      voice: 'gemini:Charon | a clear, warm university lecturer: measured, engaged, never theatrical #ctx:3a28r6'
    male|a|grave|At a threshold of 275,000 kroner per QALY nusinersen is far out of reach; at 1.4 million it is arguable — and no experiment decides that, because lambda describes the health we displace, not the drug.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 19800
      voice: 'gemini:Charon | a clear, warm university lecturer: measured, engaged, never theatrical #ctx:85o96q'
    'male|a||Across the four parts: parameters shrink with evidence, structure only in part, heterogeneity splits rather than shrinks, and the methodological core survives every trial ever run.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 13200
      voice: 'gemini:Charon | a clear, warm university lecturer: measured, engaged, never theatrical #ctx:10cvjh4'
    male|a||More money buys precision about the world; it never buys agreement about what the world is worth — and next time we look at how to show that residue honestly.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 10160
      voice: 'gemini:Charon | a clear, warm university lecturer: measured, engaged, never theatrical #ctx:2qp6iu'
    male|a||Four unknowns pull at the same nusinersen decision, and the practical question is which of them another study could actually buy away — because committees are routinely asked to wait for evidence that would never have helped.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 14920
      voice: 'gemini:Charon | a clear, warm university lecturer: measured, engaged, never theatrical'
    'male|a||Of the four boxes, take the one that was never uncertainty at all — and ask: which patient does an average ICER actually describe?':
      mp3: 
      ms: 9400
      voice: 'gemini:Charon | a clear, warm university lecturer: measured, engaged, never theatrical'
    'male|a||Averaging hides heterogeneity; put all four unknowns together — and one question: which of them can more money actually fix?':
